<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20996] mgs: ir_timeout_store() returns 0 on success</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20996</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;ir_timeout_store()&lt;/tt&gt; returns the result of &lt;tt&gt;kstrtou64()&lt;/tt&gt;, which is 0 on success. A sysfs store function must return the number of bytes that it used. Thus a write to &lt;tt&gt;mgs.MGS.ir_timeout&lt;/tt&gt; sets the value, but &lt;tt&gt;lctl set_param&lt;/tt&gt; reports a failure and exits with status 22:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;# lctl set_param mgs.MGS.ir_timeout=7
error: set_param: setting /sys/fs/lustre/mgs/MGS/ir_timeout=7: wrote only 0
error: set_param: setting 'mgs/MGS/ir_timeout'='7': Invalid argument
# lctl get_param mgs.MGS.ir_timeout
mgs.MGS.ir_timeout=7
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A script that checks the exit status of &lt;tt&gt;lctl set_param&lt;/tt&gt; thus fails, although the new value is in effect.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-8066" title="Move lustre procfs handling to sysfs and debugfs." class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-8066"&gt;LU-8066&lt;/a&gt; added the bug when it moved &lt;tt&gt;ir_timeout&lt;/tt&gt; from procfs to sysfs. The fix returns &lt;tt&gt;count&lt;/tt&gt; when &lt;tt&gt;kstrtou64()&lt;/tt&gt; succeeds.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
